# This file documents the SHAPE of a future real Postgres Trino catalog file
# and is not loaded by Trino (it does not end in .properties), mirroring
# `snowflake.properties.example` in this same directory exactly. When
# Postgres catalog wiring happens for real (see LIMITATIONS.md item 1 --
# the connector itself is real as of 2026-08-09, but this Trino-side catalog
# registration is NOT, so `route="trino"` cannot reach a Postgres data
# source yet, only `route="direct_connector"` can), copy it to
# `postgresql.properties` in THIS SAME directory (and the matching
# `infra/trino/worker/catalog/` directory -- every worker needs the same
# catalog files as the coordinator) and fill in real values.
#
# Trino auto-loads any *.properties file in a node's catalog/ directory as
# a catalog, so do not add a real postgresql.properties here until
# credentials are actually available and network access from Trino to the
# real Postgres instance has been confirmed -- exactly the same discipline
# `snowflake.properties.example`'s own comment already states.

connector.name=postgresql
connection-url=jdbc:postgresql://<host>:<port>/<database>
connection-user=<postgres-user>
connection-password=<postgres-password>
